63: ### Resource model (deliberately not L5 family packing)
64: 
65: `l5-whole-unit-envelope-per-execution-v2` is a **conservative SIM model, NOT
66: equivalent to selectCompatible L5**. L5 chooses one worker per unit/family; this
67: simulator charges the entire exported envelope on every A/B/R execution. It may
68: refuse parallelism that L5 permits. A SIM refusal proves neither L5 infeasibility
69: nor real saturation. Tests compare small candidates with the actual L5 selector.
70: 
71: - `required` preserves profiles/models/tools/accounts and slots/cpu/gpu/budget,
72:   without dividing the aggregate family budget among jobs. `unknown(reason)`
73:   never admits. `unrestricted` must be explicit for new synthetic v2 units.
74: - Empty profiles/models/accounts mean impossible intersections, never wildcard;
75:   empty tools mean no tool requirement. Missing exported metadata is unknown.
76:   Manual v1 omissions retain the legacy synthetic assumptions, explicitly marked
77:   in result diagnostics; an invalid v2 export never falls back to v1.
78: - Required workers explicitly declare model, slots/cpu/gpu/budget and any needed
79:   tools. One execution occupies one worker record; no multi-job worker packing is
80:   inferred from its slot count. Every numeric requirement/capacity is a finite,
81:   nonnegative safe integer (required slots >=1); absent capabilities are unknown.
82: - `accountCapacities` supplies known remaining slots/budget under active simulated
83:   reservations. Whole-envelope slots/budget are held per execution until actual
84:   in-memory done or confirmed stop, including late results. Budget is reserved
85:   availability, **not consumed money or cumulative provider spend**.
86:   `accountQuotas` separately limits simultaneous jobs, not slots or budget.
87: - A fence, expiration, cancellation request or knowledge invalidation is not
88:   evidence that an execution stopped. No early/double credits are granted.
89: - G2 holders are immutable family attempt/token identities or distinct external
90:   inventory entries, including worker-free family reservations awaiting validation
91:   or stop confirmation. A new conflict records every direct existing holder before
92:   fencing; partial release removes only that identity. No transitive G2 closure is
93:   inferred. A fence alone cannot release a worker-free reservation.
94: - Overlapping external claims are retained as an explicitly diagnosed incoherent
95:   inventory, not a proven valid allocation. Repeated family names do not merge
96:   entries, and a stop targets one stable entry/index. A shared key remains blocked
97:   until every entry on it has actually stopped in the fixture model.
